{
  "_readme": [
    "Authoritative pick schedule: how many class-specific options each class chooses, and at",
    "which of ITS OWN class levels. Ticket 01 of the class-choices wayfinder map.",
    "",
    "A bucket declares EITHER a compact rule {start, every, until} OR an explicit {levels: []}.",
    "generic_func.levels_for(class, bucket, class_level) expands either into a level list; the",
    "count is len(levels) and the k-th pick's level stamp is levels[k-1].",
    "",
    "  until   caps a compact rule. Load-bearing: class levels reach 40 (level_and_bab.py:19)",
    "          and nine of these lists stop at 19 or 20, so an unbounded rule would silently",
    "          over-deliver above 20th. A row with no `until` is unbounded TODAY, which is a",
    "          question ticket 03 owns, not a decision this table has made.",
    "  stamps  false where the chooser records no level stamp (generic_multi_chooser does not).",
    "  source  raw | approximation | unverified | bug | (empty rows) unswept.",
    "          `unverified` means a human authored the number and nobody has checked it against",
    "          Sieg's Guide yet -- NOT that it is wrong. `bug` means the number was never chosen",
    "          by anyone: it was defaulted at the call site. Ticket 01 ruling 5.",
    "",
    "Every rollable class has a row, so a class joining the pool without a schedule is a hard",
    "failure rather than a silence. An empty row is a VERDICT once its reason is filled in;",
    "`unswept` means ticket 02 has not reached it yet."
  ],
